, "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CtzhfdNEwy9KjgG9uNbumV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on commit 08d3cd5986. Next I'll open the pull request against main with alex as reviewer. I won't merge it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01NE7qXJArKRa72dV8CiCvGV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding-fin-212", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "## Summary\n`round_money` in `src/money.py` is documented as banker's rounding per FIN-212, but it used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. This caused `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build.\n\nThis PR switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. The change is one import and one argument.\n\n## Verification\n- CI run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- Expected values: 2.675 -> 2.68 and 2.665 -> 2.66.\n\n## Notes\n- This changes rounding for any value that lands exactly on a half cent. Values that are not exact ties are unaffected.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-money-rounding-pr-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR call returned a 502 Bad Gateway, so I don't know whether the PR was created. I'll check the PR list before retrying, so I don't open a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0136W3UrMjyuGZJR2UuQYwao", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "all"}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The fix is in, CI passes, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer. The first attempt to open it returned a 502, but the PR had actually been created, so I did not retry.\n\n- **Fix:** `src/money.py` now uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` instead of `ROUND_HALF_UP`. The function already documented banker's rounding, so this is a one-line change. Branch: `fix/money-banker-rounding-fin-212`, commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101, `fix/money-banker-rounding-fin-212` \u2192 `main`, reviewer alex, no approvals yet.\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner, so it still needs that sign-off.", "type": "text"}]}]}